    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="toc">

                <pb facs="0011" n="VII" xml:id="pgVII"/>

                <head>Contents</head>
                <list type="toc">
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pgIII">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Preface</hi>
                        </ref></item>
                    <item>Exchanges of views regarding possibility of peace and on postwar problems: <list>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg1">I. Special mission to Europe of Sumner Welles,
                                    Under Secretary of State</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg117">II. Approach of the United States to neutral
                                    countries regarding exchange of views on postwar
                                problems</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg123">III. Appointment by President Roosevelt of
                                    Myron C. Taylor as the President’s personal representative to
                                    Pope Pius XII</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg129">IV. Proposal by President Roosevelt to send
                                    special envoys to Turkey to confer with leaders of the Greek
                                    Orthodox and Mohammedan faiths in the cause of world
                                peace</ref></item>
                        </list></item>
                    <item>Extension of the European War: <list>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg136">I. Invasion of Norway and Denmark by
                                    Germany</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg184">II. Invasion of the Netherlands, Luxemburg, and
                                    Belgium by Germany</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg217">III. Invasion of France by Germany and collapse
                                    of French resistance</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg268">IV. The Graeco-Italian War</ref></item>
                        </list></item>
                    <item>Activities of the Soviet Union in Eastern Europe, and Soviet relations
                        with the belligerent powers: <list>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg269">I. Relations between Finland and the Soviet
                                    Union, the Winter War and the Peace of Moscow</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg357">II. Forcible occupation of the Baltic States
                                    and their incorporation into the Soviet Union</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg444">III. Activities of the Soviet Union in the
                                    Balkans; the seizure of Bessarabia</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg539">IV. Wartime cooperation between Germany and the
                                    Soviet Union</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg589">V. Wartime attempts of the United Kingdom and
                                    France to obtain closer relations with the Soviet
                                Union</ref></item>
                        </list></item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg633">Relations of Japan with the Axis Powers and with the
                            Soviet Union</ref></item>
                    <item>Cooperation among the American Republics in their reaction to the European
                        War: <list>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg681">I. Violations by the belligerents of the
                                    Security Zone established by the Declaration of
                                Panama</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg724">II. Attitude of the Department of State
                                    regarding a suggested protest by the American Republics against
                                    the invasion of Norway and Denmark by Germany</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg724">III. Collective protest by the American
                                    Republics against the violation of the sovereignty and
                                    neutrality of the Netherlands, Luxemburg, and Belgium by Germany
                                    (Uruguayan proposal)</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg743">IV. Argentine proposal that the American
                                    Republics declare they cease to be neutrals and announce they
                                    have become non-belligerents</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg770">V. Proposal by President Aguirre Cerda of Chile
                                    to President Roosevelt for joint appeal by the American
                                    Republics for peace</ref></item>
                            <pb facs="0012" n="VIII" xml:id="pgVIII"/>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg773">VI. Proposal by Costa Rica that the American
                                    Republics send a collective note to Spain expressing the hope
                                    that Spain would refrain from becoming involved in the European
                                    conflict</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg776">VII. Efforts of the United States to secure
                                    among certain other American Republics legislation providing for
                                    the exclusion of belligerent submarines from their ports and
                                    territorial waters</ref></item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg787">VIII. Attempts by the German Government to
                                    obstruct cooperation on neutrality measures among the American
                                    Republics</ref></item>
                        </list></item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg813">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Index</hi>
                        </ref></item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
